decision: changes-requested

**R2-N6 is fixed. R2-N5 is partially fixed.** Four blockers remain:

- **N7 — high:** [validate_scope.go:144](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-3932406016/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go:144). Dependency and descendant widening runs only for unmapped changes. Deleting `p/a` beneath surviving module `p` selects `p`, but can carry a consumer declaring `dependsOn: ["p/a"]`. Similarly, a changed gitlink matching a discovered parent module can leave its nested modules carried.
- **N8 — high:** [validate_scope.go:207](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-3932406016/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go:207). A declared dependency `"."` never matches ordinary root files. After deleting the root manifest, a self-contained consumer depending on `"."` can carry results despite changed root inputs.
- **N9 — high:** [validate_scope.go:135](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-3932406016/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go:135). Selection uses lexical paths, while `moduleOverrides` accepts symlink directories through `os.Stat`. An override aliasing module `a` can retain its old result when `a` changes. Account for resolved aliases or conservatively refuse their reuse.
- **N10 — high:** [validate.go:1423](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-3932406016/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go:1423). `material_clean` does not verify that HEAD stayed at the recorded commit. A concurrent committed fix can make checks pass while the record names the earlier failing head. Reverting that fix later can let carry reuse the false pass. Bind cleanliness and provenance to the captured head.

These findings follow from code inspection; writable scratch was unavailable for additional reproduction fixtures.

Focused and broader tests, race tests, vet, and strict artifact-check passed. Both required matrix runs failed on sandbox write restrictions. The sealed canonical result records 236 passes; fresh required-tool validation remains unmet.

Applied the review workflow, backend-go, security, documentation-style and delivery-evidence rules. No repository changes or attestation were made.

